-- title:
--   Minimal primes over ℓ avoid P(y)
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N$ and a prime $\ell$, and let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the subfield of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the expansions `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the nonzero divisors $d \mid N$. Let $y \in F$ be transcendental over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $A =$ `chartAlg N ℓ {y}` be the subalgebra of $F$, over the ring $\mathbb{Z}_\ell' =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) (a discrete valuation ring, and the localisation of $\mathbb{Z}$ at the prime $(\ell)$, by the results cited), consisting of all elements of $F$ that are integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_\ell'$-subalgebra generated by $y$; thus $A$ is the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[y]$ in $F$. Let $\mathfrak{p}$ be an ideal of $A$ lying in the minimal primes of the principal ideal generated by the image of the natural number $\ell$ in $A$. Then for every $P \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ whose reduction modulo $\ell$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)[X]$ is nonzero, the value of $P$ at $y$, regarded as an element of $A$ via the evident membership of $y$ in $A$, does not lie in $\mathfrak{p}$.
--
--   This is the Cohen–Seidenberg going-down theorem applied to the integral extension $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[y] \subseteq A$, where $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[y] \cong \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[X]$ is integrally closed and $\ell\,\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[X]$ is prime: it says that $\mathfrak{p}$ meets $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[y]$ exactly in $\ell\,\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[y]$, i.e. each irreducible component of the fibre over $\ell$ dominates the affine $y$-line over $\mathbb{F}_\ell$. It is used in the construction of the ring homomorphisms into Laurent series attached to such minimal primes, in [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_ringHom_laurentSeries_ker_eq_of_mem_minimalPrimes_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_ringHom_laurentSeries_ker_eq_of_mem_minimalPrimes_of_not_dvd).
